{
  "_comment": "REFERENCE ONLY (Ben, saved 2026-07-27). Original live n8n subflow that creates the Gmail DRAFT reply in the Spartan bookings inbox. Flow: Signature (builds the branded HTML signature) -> get RealID (fetch the real Message-ID header for the message) -> get id (assemble subject/body/from/cc/signature/message-ID) -> Code in JavaScript1 (build raw RFC-2822 MIME, threaded via In-Reply-To/References = Message-ID, base64url) -> HTTP Request (POST https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/drafts). NOTE: this is DRAFT creation only (no send). The reply_delivery='send' path reuses the same raw MIME but POSTs to /messages/send. Gmail cred: BOOKINGS 5/18/26 (id bgRJXZINuY5e6a3x). Use when building System B reply drafting + the draft/send setting.",
